  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m31-s001",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 5540,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks all. Three months in production, so results first and then the renewal."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s002",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-c",
      "startMs": 5790,
      "endMs": 11330,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Dispute handling time is down 35 percent on the three automated reason codes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s003",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-b",
      "startMs": 11580,
      "endMs": 14840,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That's the number the board will remember."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s004",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-d",
      "startMs": 15090,
      "endMs": 19870,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "And the queue API has held up. No incidents since launch."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s005",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-a",
      "startMs": 20120,
      "endMs": 24520,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Before we go further, congratulations are in order, I hear."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s006",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-b",
      "startMs": 24770,
      "endMs": 29170,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Yes. Wen became our Head of Risk on September 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s007",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-c",
      "startMs": 29420,
      "endMs": 34200,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thank you. It means the automation roadmap is officially mine now."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s008",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-a",
      "startMs": 34450,
      "endMs": 37710,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Congratulations, Wen. So, the roadmap. What's next?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s009",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-c",
      "startMs": 37960,
      "endMs": 42740,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I want all dispute reason codes covered. The long tail too."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s010",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-b",
      "startMs": 42990,
      "endMs": 44730,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Is that realistic?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s011",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-d",
      "startMs": 44980,
      "endMs": 50520,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "With the flag-only design, yes. The long tail just gets flagged less often."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s012",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-b",
      "startMs": 50770,
      "endMs": 55550,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then we roll out to all dispute reason codes in Q4."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s013",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-a",
      "startMs": 55800,
      "endMs": 58300,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Decided. Hana, the commercial side."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s014",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-e",
      "startMs": 58550,
      "endMs": 63330,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll send the renewal proposal by Friday, with Q4 scope included."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s015",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-b",
      "startMs": 63580,
      "endMs": 68740,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "And I'll sign the renewal by September 18, assuming the numbers hold."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s016",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-a",
      "startMs": 68990,
      "endMs": 71110,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Anything else from finance?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s017",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-b",
      "startMs": 71360,
      "endMs": 80700,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "One personal note. I'm moving to part-time in the new year, to care for my father. Wen will take more of the day-to-day."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s018",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-a",
      "startMs": 80950,
      "endMs": 85730,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thank you for telling us, Felix. We'll route more through Wen."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s019",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-c",
      "startMs": 85980,
      "endMs": 88100,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'm ready for it."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s020",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-d",
      "startMs": 88350,
      "endMs": 91990,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "From engineering, we'd like the model retrained quarterly."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s021",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-a",
      "startMs": 92240,
      "endMs": 95500,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "We'll include quarterly retraining in the proposal."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s022",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-e",
      "startMs": 95750,
      "endMs": 96730,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Noted."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31-s023",
      "speakerId": "m31-spk-a",
      "startMs": 96980,
      "endMs": 102900,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Great. So: all reason codes in Q4, proposal by Friday, signature by September 18."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Gullwing rollout and renewal\n\n**Date:** September 3\n**Attendees:** Alex Rivera (Larkspur Labs), Hana Sato (Larkspur Labs), Felix Amundsen (Gullwing Payments), Wen Zhao (Gullwing Payments), Yusuf Demir (Gullwing Payments)\n\n## Summary\n\nReview after three months of chargeback automation in production at Gullwing Payments, followed by the renewal discussion.\n\n## Results\n\n- Dispute handling time is down 35 percent on the three automated reason codes.\n- The disputes queue API has had no incidents since launch.\n\n## People\n\n- Wen Zhao became Gullwing's Head of Risk on September 1, and now officially owns the automation roadmap.\n- Felix is moving to part-time in the new year; Wen will take more of the day-to-day.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Roll out automation to all dispute reason codes in Q4**, including the long tail. The flag-only design means the long tail is simply flagged less often.\n- Quarterly model retraining will be included in the renewal proposal.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Hana Sato** — send the renewal proposal by Friday, with Q4 scope and quarterly retraining included.\n- **Felix Amundsen** — sign the renewal by September 18, assuming the numbers hold.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Route more day-to-day questions through Wen going forward.\n- Yusuf's engineering team asked for quarterly retraining because fraud patterns shift with the seasons.\n"
  },
